{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1121","id":4810388543,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABHri0Pw","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1121","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1121.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/1121.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/1121","number":1121,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"30004311: accepted simple-brace counterexample to Cedo Problem 9","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Accepted full negative answer to Cedó Problem 9 (OWR 51/2019, printed p.3228; problem 30004311 / OWR-17294-011). The original question asks for a finite nontrivial simple left brace with metabelian multiplicative group and abelian Sylow subgroups to be an asymmetric product of two trivial braces. The explicit order 20,000 example disproves that assertion with all hypotheses retained.\n\nPublished preprint: **[10.5281/zenodo.23441906](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23441906)**. [Zenodo record and downloads](https://zenodo.org/records/23441906) include the five-page research note and exact source/verification archive. Author: Alec Kriebel, ORCID 0009-0001-9320-500X, version 1.0.0, 17 October 2026, CC BY 4.0.\n\nThe paper gives the operations, an all-input group isomorphism to (C5^3 semidirect C2) x (C2^4 semidirect C5), additive group C5^4 x C2^5, all-ideal simplicity and every-Sylow checks. A universal presentation-independent lemma starts from the full admissible symmetric-cocycle definition, derives biadditivity and permits nonsplit primary additive groups. Two-trivial-factor products with abelian multiplicative Sylows have zero primary triple stars, while this example has (x*x)*x=x^3 nonzero. Established radical-ring, matched/asymmetric-product and orthogonal-action methods are credited.\n\nParent and three distinct independent mathematical families checked the full proof. Four unchanged exact standard-library programs pass ordinary and optimized modes, including both Python 3.14.6 and 3.12.14. The archive retains exact results, all 19,999 deterministic ideal-seed receipts, sample derivations and deliberately broken controls. The written arguments establish the universal results; no enumeration of20,000 cubed triples or formal proof certification is claimed.\n\nTwo successive fresh independent whole-package adversarial reviews passed the identical release with no required repairs: [review1](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/9b5cbcc8296bbc046ff17efc60d11de5cc15d287/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1121_30004311/reviews/package_01/REPORT.md), [review2](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/9b5cbcc8296bbc046ff17efc60d11de5cc15d287/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1121_30004311/reviews/package_02/REPORT.md). These reviewed the original scope, complete mathematics, priority/implications, meaningful computation, all five PDF pages, metadata and exact portable archive reconstruction. Review1 also independently verified all 19,999 seed transcripts and 259,858 inference steps; parent reproduced its consumer.\n\nThe extensive current primary-source audit identified no prior full answer or verified earlier full implication. This is bounded evidence, not historical-priority certification: Rump 2020/2022 full bodies and several final journal comparisons, including 2025 JPAA, were unavailable; abstracts do not exclude broader consequences. Citation coverage and the recent query-defined screen are incomplete. [Priority decision and limits](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/9b5cbcc8296bbc046ff17efc60d11de5cc15d287/draft_pr_actual_claims_1100_1200_20261017/audits/pr1121_30004311/ROOT_PRIORITY_DECISION.md).\n\nAI tools were used extensively in construction, proof development, computation, adversarial verification, literature research and writing. The paper and supplements are **unrefereed**; independent AI reviews are not external human peer review or journal acceptance. No external individual was contacted.\n\nProduction readback verified the exact reviewed files and metadata. Google Workspace CLI added exactly one DOI row at `'Math Puzzles'!A158:D158` and read it back exactly. Reviewed source head: `f86b108ac1bc024302648eee9f47f74e26c810ec`. PDF SHA256: `dc8205d726236da7d61870806ed713ba329dbf4cdfdf049e5570d967d6b7e35e`; source/verification ZIP SHA256: `8cc6e65647ff267cb2bd57e5ba5dda4cfc05f72ac11e527517131d9422a8d93d`.\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T10:03:14Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T20:44:57Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"4ebeaf5cc493661d9786980855f54c22269a60d3","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1121/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/1121/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecK